36: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
37:     """
38:     Eject content pixels from cup-shaped frames outward along each cup's tail direction.
39: 
40:     Input structure:
41:     - bg = background. Hollow cup/Y/funnel frames, each a unique border color.
42:     - Each cup has a convergent tail spike on one side and an open mouth on the opposite side.
43:     - Content pixels (a single non-border color per cup) sit inside the cup's mouth interior.
44: 
45:     Rule:
46:     - For each cup, identify its tail spike and tail direction.
47:     - Erase all content pixels from the mouth interior.
48:     - Draw a straight line of content-colored pixels from the spike outward in the tail direction,
49:       one pixel per erased content pixel; cells beyond the grid edge are dropped.
50: 
51:     Key insight: The tail spike is the unique convergent point whose outward direction is opposite
